{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359988-forces-vs-matter-house-rules","id":1359988,"title":"Forces vs Matter house rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-09T15:42:17-08:00","id":1359988,"title":"Forces vs Matter house rules","content":"Real thing that happened in my game: Mr. Moros is played by an engineer with an excellent knowledge of physics. He used a creative thaumaturgy Matter Weaving spell to lower the specific heat of some very hot concrete such that it dumped all the heat it could no longer store into the air above it and burned a guy standing on it (mostly his feet). In my games I do not ever again want to listen to physics math to ballpark what Mr. Moros just did with creative thaumaturgy, and I also don't like how Mr. Moros does things with Matter involving heat, fire, and electricity that Mr. Obrimos only wishes he could do with Forces. So its time to come up with a house rule, and I would love feedback on my idea below or other ideas.<br /> <br /> I did some searching on this forum and found a few occasions where people have discussed the Forces/Matter overlap in the past, but didn't see much in the way of ideas to better separate them. Basically the conceptual/thematic issue evolves from many players' understanding of basic physics and natural inclination to apply those ideas to the magic system, which (unfortunately, IMO) also shows up in some of the example rotes in the core rulebook (e.g. Alter Conductivity) and so the game seems to tacitly encourage.<br /> <br /> For example, Fire is under the purview of Forces, but fire is also a chemical reaction and chemical reactions are under the purview of Matter, so in many circumstances Matter ends up being about as good as working with fire as Forces. It takes a Forces master to Make fire, but a disciple of Matter can grant a material the property of being pyrophoric using a Weaving spell so that it ignites spontaneously in the presence of air. Similarly, Electricity is under the purview of Forces, but electricity only matters in the game insofar as it interacts with objects, so Matter's control over physical properties like resistance, capacitance, and charge give it de facto dominion over electricity too for many practical applications. Matter Weaving can make an object phosphorescent, thus creating light. I think you get the idea. &quot;Many Roads&quot; addresses using different Arcana to produce the same result, but my problem here is about using different Arcana to manipulate the same facets of reality -- there should not be such overlap the purviews of the different arcana. It's a problem that primarily comes up between Matter and Forces because the concept of a &quot;force&quot; is just energy interacting <i>with</i> matter; they aren't cleanly separable. Several phenomenon under the purview of Forces belong to categories of things that are under the purview of Matter and it's just too much overlap for my tastes.<br /> <br /> The best I can come up with is to emphasize that magic does not align with sleeper science, and adopt some house rules to keep Matter from stepping on Force's toes so much. Here's my idea:<ul><li>Most Matter spells (exceptions further down) cannot influence the interactions of matter with the specific items listed as under the purview of Forces (electricity, fire, heat, light, etc...). Some physical properties Matter cannot change or influence about an object (not exhausting although I sure tried):<ul><li>Flammability</li> <li>Specific Heat</li> <li>Conductivity/Resistance (good bye, Alter Conductivity, you were always too sciencey for this game)</li> <li>Electrical charge</li> <li>Capacitance</li> <li>Luminescence</li> <li>Radioactivity</li> <li>Halving-thickness (ability to absorb radiation, like lead)</li> <li>Acoustic resonance</li> </ul></li> <li>Mass (i.e. gravity, although good luck impacting it much), magnetic field strength, and magnetic polarity are still on the table for Matter.</li> <li>If Matter Patterning is used to transform one natural material into another natural material, the resulting matter has the typical properties for that type of matter. For example, Patterning cloth into lead does make it absorb radiation as normal for lead, because then it <i>is</i> lead.</li> <li>Matter Making can make matter not found in nature that interacts with Forces phenomenon as the caster sees fit.</li> <li>Matter Mage Armor does not defend against the items under the purview of Forces -- no water vapor dynamically and intelligently condensing to quench a fireball. I'm iffy on this one despite my distaste for how the Matter mage armor description sounds like imperial magic.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T16:45:28-08:00","id":1360000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359988-forces-vs-matter-house-rules#post1359988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real thing that happened in my game: Mr. Moros is played by an engineer with an excellent knowledge of physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone with a physics degree working as an engineer, I like this player already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He used a creative thaumaturgy Matter Weaving spell to lower the specific heat of some very hot concrete such that it dumped all the heat it could no longer store into the air above it and burned a guy standing on it (mostly his feet). </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the appropriate practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my games I do not ever again want to listen to physics math to ballpark what Mr. Moros just did with creative thaumaturgy, </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and I also don't like how Mr. Moros does things with Matter involving heat, fire, and electricity that Mr. Obrimos only wishes he could do with Forces. So its time to come up with a house rule, and I would love feedback on my idea below or other ideas. </div> </div> </div>Mr. Obrimos could accomplish the same thing Mr. Moros did above with Forces 1's <i>Influence Heat</i> or, at most, Forces 2's <i>Control Heat</i>. So between one and two dots fewer, I don't know why Mr. Obrimos is upset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did some searching on this forum and found a few occasions where people have discussed the Forces/Matter overlap in the past, but didn't see much in the way of ideas to better separate them. Basically the conceptual/thematic issue evolves from many players' understanding of basic physics and natural inclination to apply those ideas to the magic system, which (unfortunately, IMO) also shows up in some of the example rotes in the core rulebook (e.g. Alter Conductivity) and so the game seems to tacitly encourage. </div> </div> </div>Because while the Fallen is not the whole of reality, it is still objectively real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, Fire is under the purview of Forces, but fire is also a chemical reaction and chemical reactions are under the purview of Matter, so in many circumstances Matter ends up being about as good as working with fire as Forces. </div> </div> </div>No. A Mage with Forces can start manipulating fire at one dot, a Mage with only Matter can cause fire to occur but can't directly manipulate it ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It takes a Forces master to Make fire, but a disciple of Matter can grant a material the property of being pyrophoric using a Weaving spell so that it ignites spontaneously in the presence of air. </div> </div> </div>An Apprentice of Forces can turn a spark into a raging inferno. A Disciple of Forces could turn ambient light into fire. A Novice of Forces can turn any source of light into a beam hot enough to light pretty much anything on fire.<br /> <br /> And then they can control the fire.<br /> <br /> A Disciple of Matter can make a material combustible or flammable, but cannot control the resultant fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, Electricity is under the purview of Forces, but electricity only matters in the game insofar as it interacts with objects, so Matter's control over physical properties like resistance, capacitance, and charge give it de facto dominion over electricity too for many practical applications. </div> </div> </div>Matter can manipulate those at Matter 3. Forces has spells that let it interact with those objects at Forces 1 and 2. Seems like Forces still comes out ahead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Matter Weaving can make an object phosphorescent, thus creating light. I think you get the idea. </div> </div> </div>And Forces 2 can turn black body radiation into visible light. Again, same effect earlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Many Roads&quot; addresses using different Arcana to produce the same result, but my problem here is about using different Arcana to manipulate the same facets of reality -- there should not be such overlap the purviews of the different arcana. </div> </div> </div>Do you have a problem with both Forces and Life being able to grant flight? Death and Time being able to kill someone from old age? Prime and Fate being able to grant 9 and 8 again on spellcasting rolls?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a problem that primarily comes up between Matter and Forces because the concept of a &quot;force&quot; is just energy interacting <i>with</i> matter; they aren't cleanly separable. </div> </div> </div>That's because energy and matter are fundamentally the same. It's useful to make them different at a macro level, but they're not <i>really</i> different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Several phenomenon under the purview of Forces belong to categories of things that are under the purview of Matter and it's just too much overlap for my tastes. </div> </div> </div>Matter is capable of achieving certain, limited effects that are achievable via Forces, generally at a higher dot level and with far less precise control over the phenomena once it manifests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The best I can come up with is to emphasize that magic does not align with sleeper science, and adopt some house rules to keep Matter from stepping on Force's toes so much. </div> </div> </div>Magic doesn't align with Sleeper science, but Magic does affect objective reality. This isn't Ascension and its anti-science emphasis with its completely nonsensical and internally inconsistent &quot;subjective reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's my idea:<ul><li>Most Matter spells (exceptions further down) cannot influence the interactions of matter with the specific items listed as under the purview of Forces (electricity, fire, heat, light, etc...). Some physical properties Matter cannot change or influence about an object (not exhausting although I sure tried):<ul><li>Flammability</li> <li>Specific Heat</li> <li>Conductivity/Resistance (good bye, Alter Conductivity, you were always too sciencey for this game)</li> <li>Electrical charge</li> <li>Capacitance</li> <li>Luminescence</li> <li>Radioactivity</li> <li>Halving-thickness (ability to absorb radiation, like lead)</li> <li>Acoustic resonance</li> </ul></li> <li>Mass (i.e. gravity, although good luck impacting it much), magnetic field strength, and magnetic polarity are still on the table for Matter.</li> <li>If Matter Patterning is used to transform one natural material into another natural material, the resulting matter has the typical properties for that type of matter. For example, Patterning cloth into lead does make it absorb radiation as normal for lead, because then it <i>is</i> lead.</li> <li>Matter Making can make matter not found in nature that interacts with Forces phenomenon as the caster sees fit.</li> <li>Matter Mage Armor does not defend against the items under the purview of Forces -- no water vapor dynamically and intelligently condensing to quench a fireball. I'm iffy on this one despite my distaste for how the Matter mage armor description sounds like imperial magic.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>Whelp, you definitely aren't a physicist.<br /> <br /> Everything you want to remove from Matter is something Matter can only affect at 3 or 4 dots but Forces can deal with at 1 or 2, and deal with more directly and better in the vast majority of situations.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Edit] For me, the real grey area between Forces and Matter are Hydrogen and Helium atoms. Alpha radiation is clearly under the purview of Forces as radiation, but Helium gas is clearly Matter, but they're the same thing (Alpha radiation is just high energy). Likewise, Hydrogen gas is definitely Matter, but a single proton is Forces, but a Hydrogen+ ion is just a single proton with no electron (let's ignore deuterium and tritium for now). Obviously, these are edge cases, but it's fun to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 01-09-2020, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T16:53:54-08:00","id":1360002,"title":"","content":"The solution to this is to stop thinking about how things would work according to mundane physics and think how they would work according to Supernal magic. For something like the spell to change how concrete holds/transmits heat, I'd compare what a spell of that level would be capable of to the existing spell 'Alter Conductivity'. It would increase/decrease the amount of heat said section of concrete could hold/transmit by 2 per point of potency, limited by whatever direct form of heat you, the ST, decide it is directly connected to, advanced math not needed. If you decide that from a magic standpoint this random section of concrete that has been in the sun all day is only holding 1L worth of heat (possibly judging things based on Forces Transform energy table) then it only holds 1L of damage, mundane physics be damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T17:50:28-08:00","id":1360010,"title":"","content":"The Matter mage can only manipulate forces that are already there. They cannot direct, transform or alter said forces without jumping through significant hoops, by altering the matter that surrounds those forces. That is fine, because a Force mage will do it faster, easier and with more precision, leaving more Reach open.<br /> <br /> An Obrimos says &quot;Lightning, you strike right there !&quot;, it answers &quot;YES SIR !&quot; and he calibrates it just right to incapacitate a target.<br /> <br /> A Moros tries the same, but then notices he needs to make a lightning rod, make it conducive and then hope the checks they prepared were enough to avoid causing permanent damage.<br /> <br /> Convenience is the balancing factor: the time, Reach and spell control required to replicate another Arcana's specialty. Making heavy rain is extremely difficult for a master of Fate, but laughably simple for one of Forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:10:56-08:00","id":1360016,"title":"","content":"You can manipulate the fire directly, or you can manipulate the flammability and caloric content of what it's burning. You can call lightning, or you can give something high positive charge and the lightning (or electric current from whatever its touching) will find it. Forces always act on something; if you configure the something correctly then the laws of the fallen world will handle the forces part for you -- sometimes more effectively than using Forces magic.<br /> <br /> But I'm not really bothered by which one is more effective; I'm bothered by Matter having so much to do with manipulating the same things as Forces. It's a degree of redundancy and overlap that doesn't exist between any other two paths. It robs Forces of too much of its own uniqueness and flavor. Sometimes what you want to do with Fire takes more dots with Matter than Forces, sometimes less, I don't care. I care that Matter and Forces both manipulate the chemical reaction we call fire even though fire is called out as belonging to Forces. It's not about balance, it's about having two Arcana that are very distinct rather than heavily overlapping.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Is there any other case where the rulebook gives a rote for one arcana that manipulates a phenomenon explicitly listed as belonging to another arcana without requiring conjunctional casting? They couldn't come up with stuff for Matter to do without (haha) stealing Force's thunder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 01-09-2020, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:08:06-08:00","id":1360036,"title":"","content":"I can't wait until you discover the existence of the Spirit Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:10:44-08:00","id":1360038,"title":"","content":"Sounds more like a table problem than a rules problem to me. Maybe the dude with Forces could ask the guy with Matter for some sweet tips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:14:32-08:00","id":1360041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359988-forces-vs-matter-house-rules?p=1360038#post1360038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like a table problem than a rules problem to me. Maybe the dude with Forces could ask the guy with Matter for some sweet tips.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the right answer. I'm a marketing guy who doesn't know the first thing about physics, but thankfully one of my players is taking his Masters degree in Inorganic Chemistry, so I mine him for ideas all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T21:37:48-08:00","id":1360052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359988-forces-vs-matter-house-rules?p=1360036#post1360036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't wait until you discover the existence of the Spirit Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the condescension, but I'm aware of it already. There's a big thematic difference between persuading spirits to use numina that replicate some of the effects of supernal magic and outright controlling the flagship phenomenon from purview of one arcanum using supernal magic from another arcanum. For one thing, you actually have to do the legwork to cultivate the relevant spirits and for a second it doesn't compromise the unique flavor of any other arcanum.<br /> <br /> Anyway I can see I'm not going to get any useful feedback about e.g. unforeseen consequences with that houserule so we'll just try it out in play and see how it works out. I don't need to read a rehash of the same argument I already read in the forum's history.<br /> <br /> This forum: Arcana don't follow the laws and assumption of sleeper science, they go by mysterious supernal truths that often defy those false realities.<br /> Also this forum: Having a strong science background really helps in coming up with creative thaumaturgy spells, don't play an Obrimos or Moros without one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 01-10-2020, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T22:14:21-08:00","id":1360059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359988-forces-vs-matter-house-rules?p=1360052#post1360052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the condescension, but I'm aware of it already. There's a big thematic difference between persuading spirits to use numina that replicate some of the effects of supernal magic and outright controlling the flagship phenomenon from purview of one arcanum using supernal magic from another arcanum. For one thing, you actually have to do the legwork to cultivate the relevant spirits and for a second it doesn't compromise the unique flavor of any other arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter doesn't compromise the unique flavor of Forces, either. For some reason you seem to believe that altering the physical properties of matter so that a secondary effect occurs is the same as directly controlling that effect with Forces. It's not, you don't have any direct control of any fire created as a secondary effect of altered matter properties. Comparatively speaking, it's easier to use an electricity spirit or a fire spirit than to use Matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway I can see I'm not going to get any useful feedback about e.g. unforeseen consequences with that houserule so we'll just try it out in play and see how it works out. I don't need to read a rehash of the same argument I already read in the forum's history. </div> </div> </div>Here are the forseeable consequences: you'll probably irritate the player who invested in Matter based on how it was presented in the book, and magic will work in a less logical way as none of the things you're banning are under the purview of Forces (except electrical charge, but Matter can only mess with that directly with Patterning by changing an atom into an ion of that atom).<ul><li>Flammability - Forces controls fire, not flammability.</li> <li>Specific Heat - Forces controls heat, not the capacity to store energy.</li> <li>Conductivity/Resistance (good bye, Alter Conductivity, you were always too sciencey for this game) - Forces controls electrons, not the ability of electrons to flow through matter.</li> <li>Electrical charge - this isn't really under Matter except insofar as Matter Patterning can change an atom into an ion.</li> <li>Capacitance - see Conductivity/Resistance.</li> <li>Luminescence - Forces controls light, not the emission thereof per se (though since forces can control electrons, you could do a pretty good approximation of a free electron laser with just Forces).</li> <li>Radioactivity - Forces controls radiation, not whether matter is radioactive.</li> <li>Halving-thickness (ability to absorb radiation, like lead) - Forces controls radiation, not absorption thereof.</li> <li>Acoustic resonance - Forces controls sound, not the ability of matter to propagate sound.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This forum: Arcana don't follow the laws and assumption of sleeper science, they go by mysterious supernal truths that often defy those false realities.<br /> Also this forum: Having a strong science background really helps in coming up with creative thaumaturgy spells, don't play an Obrimos or Moros without one! </div> </div> </div>The ability to defy false realities does not preclude the ability to exploit them.<br /> <br /> <br /> None of us here can stop you from implementing your house rules. But don't you think it's telling that we all think they're bad house rules and that you are fundamentally misunderstanding the Arcana in question?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [Edit] And now that I stop to think on it, reducing the specific heat of an object wouldn't cause it to expel the energy, it'd cause the object to melt or burst apart depending on its composition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 01-10-2020, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T22:32:15-08:00","id":1360063,"title":"","content":"I actually wouldn't allow changing electrical charge, but other than that everything else seems legitimate.<br /> <br /> Mages that tweak laws and let reality ensue are just being creative.<br /> <br /> The forces mage could cause lightning to strike sand and create fulgurite. <br /> Or they could create heat enough for metal to melt.<br /> Or create a sound that shatters glass due to hitting the right note. <br /> There was a bridge that collapsed to vibrations created by the wind at a particular speed. It was a construction flaw (that modern bridges are engineered to not have) <br /> Matter overlap? Nah, just creative.<br /> <br /> Maybe just make the character make an intelligence + science roll to calculate potential side effects or magnitude of the effect?<br /> <br /> I particularly like using life to grant axolotl traits. The end result is lasting regeneration... But it takes a long time to happen.<br /> Or use life to give tardigrade traits. Radiation resistance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Think of the magic duel from disney's the sword in the Stone. Merlin won by turning into a viral disease, while his opponent had no idea. If she knew enough about animals and biology she could have turned into a life form that was immune or unaffected by the disease, but she didn't know any. Admittedly the disease affected dragons and humans in the same way so it might have been a bit hard. Still, it's a nice example of a mage leveraging knowledge of fallen laws to their advantage. Also fun to rewatch <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","user":"MovingMind","date":". 01-10-2020, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T09:00:27-08:00","id":1360133,"title":"","content":"Have you tried to talking to your players? Is this actually a problem for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T10:07:43-08:00","id":1360148,"title":"","content":"Whatever the approach, there will always be an overlap in Arcana. But I don't think invalidating most of the the Practice of Weaving, save for a few arbitrary exceptions, is a satisfying solution. Mage is all about flexibility and creativity, so weakening an Arcanum like that might not feel good for the players who invested in it.<br /> <br /> The important distinction is how players approach the Arcanum, how their characters think about it and adapt it to their shadow names.<br /> <br /> Lets take an example: Vice. A member of the Concord of Serpents thinks its suposed to be used as the adversary of virtue, to refine it by trials. A Clavicularius sees vice as something that needs to be made subservient to virtue, as something to be tamed. A Bene Asmodai sees it as just another part of the self, which must be entreated and indulged so that it actually helps when something important happens. Those 3 are Mind specialists, all of them focused on vice. Yet their behavior and spellcasting will be very different to reflect their different trains of thought.<br /> <br /> In essence, don't worry too much about the things they improvise. Its in the broad strokes, preparations (tools, enhanced items, etc) and pursuit of Obsession that their signature styles will emerge. If they generally follow a certain approach, it might be grounds for a Cabal Theme, which can also be pretty cool (like technomancy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T10:37:08-08:00","id":1360158,"title":"","content":"On the thing where we talk about magic is more than science. We typically say that in response to someone who is trying to make a spell not work because the science says it shouldn't.<br /> <br /> You're getting essentially the same response here. Stop messing with the magic just because someone is creative enough to exploit science to make their spells do stuff.<br /> <br /> So, it's actually not a contradiction. The answer you'll generally get is, let the magic happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:28:16-08:00","id":1360171,"title":"","content":"I tend to take an opposite approach here to a lot of posters.<br /> <br /> Science is not a skill rolled for spellcasting. Even Matter spells are rolled with Gnosis - how well you see past the illusion of the material world, not how well you embrace it. Thus, your - player or character - knowledge of science is not a factor in the effectiveness of your magic. Magic, after all, is about transcending the mundane, not embracing it. I might use the heat capacity of concrete to explain why the Matter spell caused an explosion when it paradoxed - the lie and the abyss tainting the intention of the spell - but I wouldn't allow it to <i>be </i>the intention of the spell.<br /> <br /> Matter has a purview of alchemy, gases, solids, liquids, shaping, crafting, transmutation, stasis. Burning people with hot concrete just... doesn't really fit with that. I'm not terribly interested in arguments by players about why it scientifically follows from other capabilities - the Supernal is not fundamentally scientific. An imago to burn a guy standing on hot concrete is an imago about manipulating heat, not about manipulating concrete.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> On a more game level, I tend to frown on players trying to stretch an arcanum's purview. It centralizes the game around the most creative player, makes it harder for people the other players to feel like they can really contribute. I've been on the 'winning' side of that frequently enough, and while it was fun for me, it was to the detriment of the group.<br /> <br /> So yes, I agree this is a table problem. But I don't necessarily think it's the Obrimos' problem - feeling resentful that someone else is reducing the specialness of your character by edging in on their deal (without spending any additional XP) is a genuine problem. Maybe the solution is to talk with the Obrimos, if you don't feel it's reasonable. Maybe it's to talk with the Moros, to tell them not to steal other people's thunder.<br /> <br /> But either way, chastisizing an ST for looking out for the quieter, less creative players at their table leaves me with a big frown. Social dynamics is important, and in Mage, I find that restricting arcana - forcing people to rely on the rest of their group and the rest of world - is one of the stronger tools at my disposal to spread the spotlight around a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:51:43-08:00","id":1360177,"title":"","content":"On the science thing:<br /> <br /> 1) The idea was rolling Science to see if the character, rather than the player, would actually know the laws of the Fallen World necessary to accomplish some of the stuff you can when you mix the Matter Arcanum with physics and chemistry. That is, does the character have the knowledge to form an imago of &quot;concrete releases the heat it's built up soaking up the sun,&quot; vs. the more obvious, &quot;move the heat from the concrete to the person standing on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Science is an extremely common Skill for Rotes precisely because so many spells work better with that understanding. Magic is not about transcending the mundane, it's about bringing the Supernal to the Fallen world. Magic can do this by forcibly overriding the Fallen to their desires, or by mixing the Supernal and Fallen together. It's sort of the whole philosophic basis of how the Free Council approaches magic: the mundane is magical if you know how to tap into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T12:28:33-08:00","id":1360184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1359988-forces-vs-matter-house-rules?p=1360177#post1360177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the science thing:<br /> <br /> 1) The idea was rolling Science to see if the character, rather than the player, would actually know the laws of the Fallen World necessary to accomplish some of the stuff you can when you mix the Matter Arcanum with physics and chemistry. That is, does the character have the knowledge to form an imago of &quot;concrete releases the heat it's built up soaking up the sun,&quot; vs. the more obvious, &quot;move the heat from the concrete to the person standing on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Science is an extremely common Skill for Rotes precisely because so many spells work better with that understanding. Magic is not about transcending the mundane, it's about bringing the Supernal to the Fallen world. Magic can do this by forcibly overriding the Fallen to their desires, or by mixing the Supernal and Fallen together. It's sort of the whole philosophic basis of how the Free Council approaches magic: the mundane is magical if you know how to tap into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt that was incentivised as well. One of the coolest things about Compelling is that it can take a mild, mundane version of something and make it into a stronger Condition. For example, if someone is drowsing off or sleeping lightly, then a Compelling of Mind can make it into a deep sleep, which means far more Reach to play around with than Sleep of the Just. So I understood that a skilled mage also knew how to work with the Fallen, to nudge things in just the right way to make their spell work much simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-10-2020, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T13:48:40-08:00","id":1360196,"title":"","content":"To build on what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> are saying, there is also a difference between direct and indirect effects.<br /> <br /> The Mage's ultimate goal in altering conductivity might be to zap their opponent, but that's not the goal of the spell or its imago. The primary effect of the spell (altering conductivity) does not require science to understand because it's a fundamental aspect of Matter and that's represented by your dots in Matter. What science knowledge does is predict the Fallen world consequences of your Supernal imposition, it's a secondary, non-magical effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T18:23:02-08:00","id":1360251,"title":"","content":"I was thinking some more about this, and it\u2019s actually kind of funny how much the Moros -overthought- this. Like if he just wanted to damage the guy\u2019s feet he could have just had his shoes constrict them, or perhaps less obviously have the metal shanks in the sole give out from \u201cstress,\u201d snap, and go through the guy\u2019s feet. The mechanical outcome would be just about identical to what he did. This actually makes it even harder for me to see the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}